    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 Find roofers\nPulls Google Maps listings for the search term and city. In **mock** mode this reads a saved sample of 50 Dallas roofers, so the demo runs offline. In **apify** mode it calls the Apify Google Maps scraper.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "a0340000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        640,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 Audit website + speed\nFetches each homepage and checks it: loads? mobile-friendly? online booking? click-to-call? Then asks Google PageSpeed for the mobile speed score.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "a0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1090,
        640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 Claude audit + opener\nClaude reads the facts and recent reviews, then writes the findings, a one-line cold-email opener and a short pitch. Mock mode uses a template instead.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "a0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2000,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 Score, rank, export\nEach lead gets a 0-100 opportunity score (hot / warm / cold), the list is ranked, and leads.json and leads.csv are written to the output folder.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 220,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "a0370000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
      "name": "Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
